1
00:00:01,270 --> 00:00:08,150
The new morning we've finally found

2
00:00:01,270 --> 00:00:08,150
Yatto mitsuketa atarashii asa wa

3
00:00:08,150 --> 00:00:12,190
is being hampered by the past.

4
00:00:08,150 --> 00:00:12,190
Tsukihi ga jama wo suru

5
00:00:12,390 --> 00:00:17,660
What we chased after wasn't the future,

6
00:00:12,390 --> 00:00:17,660
Mukau saki wa tsugi ja nakute

7
00:00:17,660 --> 00:00:21,490
but the past so full of remorse.

8
00:00:17,660 --> 00:00:21,490
Sugi bakari oikaketa

9
00:00:22,870 --> 00:00:27,960
The ruthless memories won't stop playing;

10
00:00:22,870 --> 00:00:27,960
Nariyamanai yousha nai omoide tachi wa

11
00:00:27,960 --> 00:00:32,050
they won't be forgiving us for a long time.

12
00:00:27,960 --> 00:00:32,050
Yurushite kuresou nimonai

13
00:00:33,340 --> 00:00:37,890
It's about now that a teardrop

14
00:00:33,340 --> 00:00:37,890
Sorosoro kana tesaguri tsukareta hoho wo

15
00:00:37,890 --> 00:00:42,560
beings to roll down my fatigued cheeks.

16
00:00:37,890 --> 00:00:42,560
Kattou ga koboreochiru

17
00:00:42,890 --> 00:00:47,810
Will this rain ever stop?

18
00:00:42,890 --> 00:00:47,810
Ame wa itsuka yamunodeshouka

19
00:00:47,810 --> 00:00:53,030
I've been freezing for a long time.

20
00:00:47,810 --> 00:00:53,030
Zuibun nagai aida tsumetai

21
00:00:53,030 --> 00:00:58,320
Why does the rain continue to fix on me?

22
00:00:53,030 --> 00:00:58,320
Ame wa doushite boku wo erabuno

23
00:00:58,320 --> 00:01:03,080
I wonder if it could embrace me.

24
00:00:58,320 --> 00:01:03,080
Tsutsumarete iikana

25
00:01:03,080 --> 00:01:07,870
Today, the rain falls again;

26
00:01:03,080 --> 00:01:07,870
Ame wa yamu koto wo shirazuni

27
00:01:07,870 --> 00:01:13,090
endlessly it falls knowing no end.

28
00:01:07,870 --> 00:01:13,090
Kyou mo furitsuzukukeredo

29
00:01:13,090 --> 00:01:18,130
We nestle close to each other to share the warmth

30
00:01:13,090 --> 00:01:18,130
Sotto sashidashita kasa no naka de

31
00:01:18,680 --> 00:01:29,850
under this umbrella, you gently held out to me.

32
00:01:18,680 --> 00:01:29,850
Nukumori ni yorisoinagara

33
00:01:31,230 --> 00:01:33,020
What the hell is going on?

34
00:01:32,320 --> 00:01:33,480
What happened?!

35
00:01:33,480 --> 00:01:34,360
I don't know.

36
00:01:34,360 --> 00:01:36,700
I heard Colonel Mustang did something.

37
00:01:36,700 --> 00:01:37,780
Are you serious?

38
00:01:37,780 --> 00:01:38,990
Well, it's just a rumor I heard.

39
00:01:39,660 --> 00:01:42,030
Hey! Turn on the radio!

40
00:01:42,370 --> 00:01:44,240
"Radio Capital"!

41
00:01:44,240 --> 00:01:46,080
Radio Capital?

42
00:01:46,080 --> 00:01:48,870
Yeah! There's something crazy going on!

43
00:01:48,870 --> 00:01:51,710
That station is so lame.

44
00:01:51,710 --> 00:01:52,790
Just do it!

45
00:01:52,790 --> 00:01:54,920
Before the military stops the broadcast!

46
00:01:54,920 --> 00:01:55,840
Hurry!

47
00:01:59,550 --> 00:02:02,350
Is that right, Madam?

48
00:02:02,350 --> 00:02:04,100
The Führer President's wife?

49
00:02:04,970 --> 00:02:05,930
Yes.

50
00:02:06,640 --> 00:02:10,350
The Central Army tried to murder me.

51
00:02:11,130 --> 00:02:14,130
Flame of Vengeance

52
00:02:11,130 --> 00:02:14,130
Flame of Vengeance

53
00:02:14,110 --> 00:02:18,740
So they pointed a gun at you to shoot you dead?

54
00:02:18,900 --> 00:02:20,110
That's right.

55
00:02:21,200 --> 00:02:25,990
He said, "Kill her along with Colonel Mustang's men."

56
00:02:26,910 --> 00:02:30,000
I've heard that Führer President Bradley is currently in the east for an inspection,

57
00:02:30,120 --> 00:02:32,750
and is not in Central at the moment.

58
00:02:33,040 --> 00:02:34,250
Yes.

59
00:02:34,250 --> 00:02:37,420
So do you suppose someone in the upper echelon

60
00:02:37,550 --> 00:02:39,670
is planning a coup d'etat while the Führer President is absent?

61
00:02:40,090 --> 00:02:42,010
I can't say for sure.

62
00:02:42,300 --> 00:02:44,350
Is this truly the real Madam?

63
00:02:44,350 --> 00:02:47,060
I recognize this voice, though. She's real.

64
00:02:45,930 --> 00:02:51,690
But Madam, the fact that your son was also not in Central at the time is...

65
00:02:51,690 --> 00:02:53,900
I can't get in touch with my son either!

66
00:02:53,900 --> 00:02:54,520
What?!

67
00:02:55,320 --> 00:02:56,610
You've gotta be kidding me!

68
00:02:57,780 --> 00:02:59,150
Poor thing...

69
00:02:59,650 --> 00:03:01,610
I hope Selim's safe and sound.

70
00:03:01,610 --> 00:03:03,660
Please get yourself together, Madam Bradley.

71
00:03:03,370 --> 00:03:04,700
A coup d'etat, they say!

72
00:03:04,700 --> 00:03:07,490
In any case, we are thankful that you're safe and sound.

73
00:03:04,700 --> 00:03:08,160
Do you think anyone other than Bradley would be able to keep this nation together?

74
00:03:08,620 --> 00:03:15,000
If Colonel Mustang hadn't saved me,
I don't even know if I'd be here right now...

75
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:20,050
I see, so Colonel Mustang had already predicted the coup d'etat.

76
00:03:18,710 --> 00:03:20,380
Mustang, huh...?

77
00:03:21,220 --> 00:03:26,300
Well then, could you please describe in detail of what happened when you were rescued?

78
00:03:26,810 --> 00:03:27,680
Of course.

79
00:03:28,220 --> 00:03:33,020
Have you still not told her that Selim is a homunculus?

80
00:03:30,230 --> 00:03:34,850
A gun was pointed at me, so I closed my eyes and began saying my prayers to God.

81
00:03:33,020 --> 00:03:34,270
How could we?

82
00:03:35,060 --> 00:03:38,190
She doesn't even know that her husband is currently missing.

83
00:03:35,480 --> 00:03:39,400
When I heard a gun go off, I thought everything was over.

84
00:03:39,940 --> 00:03:40,690
But-

85
00:03:42,400 --> 00:03:45,320
We hadn't told you this yet, Madam,

86
00:03:45,320 --> 00:03:51,660
but the thing is, the train that the Führer President was on yesterday in the east was bombed by someone.

87
00:03:51,660 --> 00:03:52,580
What?

88
00:03:52,580 --> 00:03:55,290
He is currently missing.

89
00:04:00,130 --> 00:04:01,210
Madam Bradley!

90
00:04:02,880 --> 00:04:03,970
Are you all right?!

91
00:04:04,630 --> 00:04:10,720
I-It appears as though Madam Bradley is feeling ill due to shock.

92
00:04:11,180 --> 00:04:16,020
But the Führer President has gone missing?
What could this mean?

93
00:04:19,020 --> 00:04:23,360
Colonel Mustang has always been leery of the upper echelon,

94
00:04:23,740 --> 00:04:26,870
and was anticipating that they'd pull something.

95
00:04:27,450 --> 00:04:29,490
And that's when the Führer President's train was bombed,

96
00:04:29,490 --> 00:04:33,290
and on top of that, an order to shoot the Madam was given.

97
00:04:33,710 --> 00:04:35,580
Everything is clear now.

98
00:04:36,170 --> 00:04:40,590
There is a faction in the upper echelon that wants to get rid of the Führer President.

99
00:04:41,090 --> 00:04:42,090
Fool!

100
00:04:42,920 --> 00:04:44,970
Hurry up and stop the broadcast!

101
00:04:44,970 --> 00:04:47,840
Be well-prepared for the consequences if you refuse!

102
00:04:48,090 --> 00:04:51,100
But we can't!

103
00:04:51,350 --> 00:04:57,850
They've taken hostages, and we can hardly move due to the fact that they've got a gun on us!

104
00:04:57,850 --> 00:05:02,820
And for starters, there are so many of them that we don't know what to do!

105
00:05:03,360 --> 00:05:05,490
Let me talk to Mustang!

106
00:05:05,490 --> 00:05:07,360
I'll talk to him directly!

107
00:05:07,530 --> 00:05:08,240
Huh?

108
00:05:08,240 --> 00:05:10,240
The... Colonel?

109
00:05:18,670 --> 00:05:20,080
Don't shoot!

110
00:05:21,000 --> 00:05:23,340
Forgive me! Please!

111
00:05:34,810 --> 00:05:36,100
How did you like my acting?

112
00:05:36,100 --> 00:05:37,230
It was perfect!

113
00:05:37,480 --> 00:05:40,270
Okay, keep the show airing!

114
00:05:40,310 --> 00:05:40,770
Sir!

115
00:05:41,230 --> 00:05:44,230
Like we can let a scoop like this go!

116
00:05:44,400 --> 00:05:47,570
Next, we will have one of Colonel Mustang's subordinates speak with us.

117
00:05:47,570 --> 00:05:50,160
She also participated in the mission to rescue the Madam.

118
00:05:49,160 --> 00:05:52,120
So it wasn't the Colonel who planned the coup d'etat.

119
00:05:53,030 --> 00:05:57,410
We, who support Colonel Mustang, have very little influence...

120
00:05:57,410 --> 00:05:59,080
This... voice!

121
00:05:57,410 --> 00:05:59,370
...but inheriting the Führer President's will,

122
00:05:59,710 --> 00:06:03,880
we are prepared to stand up to our underhanded opponents with everything we've got,

123
00:06:03,880 --> 00:06:04,920
in the name of justice.

124
00:06:11,720 --> 00:06:13,300
That damned Mustang.

125
00:06:13,300 --> 00:06:18,770
Now that Bradley isn't around, he's exploiting the hell out of the Führer President's influence.

126
00:06:19,310 --> 00:06:21,810
And bringing up words like 'justice'...

127
00:06:22,650 --> 00:06:26,530
It would be nice if the people would take his bait.

128
00:06:27,190 --> 00:06:28,530
You sounded like you're used to this kind of stuff.

129
00:06:29,990 --> 00:06:33,580
I'm surprised you could use a silly and vague word like 'justice'.

130
00:06:33,580 --> 00:06:34,910
It's fine.

131
00:06:34,910 --> 00:06:37,540
Everyone loves justice.

132
00:06:37,750 --> 00:06:38,960
She's right.

133
00:06:38,960 --> 00:06:40,790
The first person to say it wins.

134
00:06:42,330 --> 00:06:44,170
What the hell is going on?

135
00:06:44,710 --> 00:06:47,300
I heard it's not Mustang and his men's doing.

136
00:06:47,300 --> 00:06:49,090
Is that really true?

137
00:06:49,550 --> 00:06:52,140
Roy Mustang is telling the truth.

138
00:06:53,050 --> 00:06:55,470
We just arrived here from the east,

139
00:06:55,470 --> 00:07:00,100
but there was a huge ruckus over there
about the Führer President's train being blown up.

140
00:07:00,600 --> 00:07:04,360
Do the people at Central still not know about it?

141
00:07:04,520 --> 00:07:09,610
The highest-ranking man in the nation is missing, and they still haven't bothered to tell its people anything?

142
00:07:09,860 --> 00:07:12,110
So it really is a coup d'etat?!

143
00:07:12,110 --> 00:07:13,490
Who's the mastermind?

144
00:07:13,490 --> 00:07:16,620
If Radio Capital happens to be ambushed and the Madam gets killed,

145
00:07:16,620 --> 00:07:18,370
it's obviously the upper echelon who's behind it all!

146
00:07:18,370 --> 00:07:20,290
What happened to Selim?!

147
00:07:20,290 --> 00:07:22,170
He's probably being taken hostage!

148
00:07:22,170 --> 00:07:23,880
I hope he's still alive...

149
00:07:30,260 --> 00:07:32,260
What the hell are the guards doing?!

150
00:07:32,260 --> 00:07:33,340
Sir!

151
00:07:33,340 --> 00:07:36,760
Apparently, the enemy was in possession of more firearms than they'd expected,

152
00:07:36,850 --> 00:07:38,890
and they're putting up a bitter fight.

153
00:07:38,890 --> 00:07:42,890
There has to be limit to how many firearms they can carry!

154
00:07:43,690 --> 00:07:45,400
We have a call from the guards.

155
00:07:46,770 --> 00:07:47,570
Here, sir.

156
00:07:48,150 --> 00:07:49,650
What took you so long to contact us?!

157
00:07:49,650 --> 00:07:51,190
What is going on over there?!

158
00:07:51,190 --> 00:07:51,820
Over!

159
00:07:52,030 --> 00:07:55,110
W-We had no idea the men from Briggs were in possession of such-

160
00:07:56,620 --> 00:07:58,080
H-Hey!

161
00:08:00,330 --> 00:08:02,500
W-Will we be okay?

162
00:08:02,870 --> 00:08:06,080
There's no way they'll take control of this place, right?

163
00:08:06,080 --> 00:08:07,090
Of course!

164
00:08:08,090 --> 00:08:10,590
Seriously... what fools.

165
00:08:11,010 --> 00:08:13,050
They're going to have to bring in something like a tank to-

166
00:08:14,300 --> 00:08:14,970
Huh?

167
00:08:16,760 --> 00:08:17,470
What?!

168
00:08:21,140 --> 00:08:24,310
Shall I lend you a hand, Fullmetal?

169
00:08:24,480 --> 00:08:25,690
Colonel!

170
00:08:27,860 --> 00:08:31,030
Looks like you've made some new friends.

171
00:08:33,490 --> 00:08:34,570
Scar.

172
00:08:37,740 --> 00:08:40,620
But wow, this place brings back memories, Lieutenant.

173
00:08:40,620 --> 00:08:42,700
It reminds me of your crying face.

174
00:08:43,500 --> 00:08:46,290
I'd like to see honest tears like that from you again someday.

175
00:08:47,000 --> 00:08:49,790
I thought you despised liquids.

176
00:08:49,790 --> 00:08:51,300
Since they make you useless.

177
00:08:53,800 --> 00:08:55,680
Save the chatting for later!

178
00:08:55,680 --> 00:08:56,510
Take them down!

179
00:08:56,760 --> 00:08:58,680
Don't you order me around!

180
00:08:58,680 --> 00:08:59,680
Roger!

181
00:08:59,680 --> 00:09:01,470
We need to defeat these pale things, right?

182
00:09:03,270 --> 00:09:04,640
It's useless, Lieutenant!

183
00:09:04,640 --> 00:09:06,730
Bullets aren't enough to bring them down!

184
00:09:07,440 --> 00:09:08,560
That again?!

185
00:09:08,560 --> 00:09:09,900
Why does this always happen?

186
00:09:11,110 --> 00:09:12,320
Homunculi?

187
00:09:13,900 --> 00:09:16,530
No, their wounds aren't recovering.

188
00:09:17,280 --> 00:09:18,740
But they don't die.

189
00:09:19,410 --> 00:09:21,080
Must be the power of a philosopher's stone.

190
00:10:00,820 --> 00:10:03,490
They are enemies, Fullmetal.

191
00:10:12,340 --> 00:10:14,380
Running around like a cockroach...!

192
00:10:15,380 --> 00:10:18,050
Seems like he doesn't want me going this way.

193
00:10:18,550 --> 00:10:20,050
That sensation also grows larger as I go...

194
00:10:20,260 --> 00:10:21,050
It has to be...!

195
00:10:50,290 --> 00:10:51,460
Is that you, May?!

196
00:10:54,840 --> 00:10:55,960
Envy!

197
00:10:56,960 --> 00:10:58,090
You guys...!

198
00:11:01,930 --> 00:11:02,890
Fool!

199
00:11:02,890 --> 00:11:04,640
Why didn't you return to your country?!

200
00:11:06,890 --> 00:11:07,770
But...

201
00:11:08,140 --> 00:11:09,310
B-

202
00:11:09,310 --> 00:11:10,560
Because...!

203
00:11:10,560 --> 00:11:12,100
It's fine. Don't cry.

204
00:11:12,520 --> 00:11:14,730
I'm so sorry, Mister Scar!

205
00:11:15,570 --> 00:11:16,610
Man...

206
00:11:17,070 --> 00:11:20,780
Human traits like this make my skin crawl.

207
00:11:24,570 --> 00:11:28,910
But wow, looks like you guys showed them who's boss.

208
00:11:29,790 --> 00:11:33,670
The Fullmetal Alchemist and the Flame Alchemist.

209
00:11:33,670 --> 00:11:35,250
In addition, Scar.

210
00:11:35,670 --> 00:11:39,300
The shitty chimeras I owe a favor to from up north are with you too.

211
00:11:39,300 --> 00:11:43,470
Now... I wonder who I should take care of first.

212
00:11:43,470 --> 00:11:44,800
So you're Envy?

213
00:11:46,180 --> 00:11:48,810
You're the Homunculus that can change form, right?

214
00:11:49,350 --> 00:11:51,770
Oh, you know about me?

215
00:11:52,270 --> 00:11:55,060
Nice to meet you, Colonel Mustang.

216
00:11:55,060 --> 00:11:56,230
Wait, huh?

217
00:11:56,730 --> 00:11:58,570
Is this okay, Scar?

218
00:11:58,570 --> 00:12:02,150
He's a State Alchemist who turned Ishbal into hell.

219
00:12:03,240 --> 00:12:04,660
You're right.

220
00:12:06,320 --> 00:12:08,240
What, you're all buddy-buddy now?

221
00:12:08,780 --> 00:12:10,410
This is boring.

222
00:12:10,620 --> 00:12:13,620
Show me something more muddy and disgusting.

223
00:12:13,920 --> 00:12:18,540
I find enjoyment in watching you pieces of trash shrieking like animals.

224
00:12:21,090 --> 00:12:24,050
I don't have time to entertain your vulgar hobbies.

225
00:12:24,220 --> 00:12:25,470
Vulgar?

226
00:12:26,050 --> 00:12:27,800
Well then, let me ask.

227
00:12:28,050 --> 00:12:34,560
Don't you humans also love watching people's unhappiness and watching fools dance?

228
00:12:35,440 --> 00:12:38,060
Isn't that why you're always fighting wars?

229
00:12:40,150 --> 00:12:43,990
True, it is indeed entertaining to watch fools dance like madmen.

230
00:12:46,530 --> 00:12:52,250
It's especially entertaining to watch fools like you homunculi dance.

231
00:12:54,750 --> 00:12:56,870
Well, I answered your question.

232
00:12:57,750 --> 00:13:00,250
Now it's time for you to answer mine.

233
00:13:02,260 --> 00:13:04,380
Who killed Maes Hughes?

234
00:13:06,180 --> 00:13:08,140
Answer me, Homunculus.

235
00:13:14,270 --> 00:13:15,770
Maria Ross.

236
00:13:16,230 --> 00:13:17,690
The one you burned to a crisp.

237
00:13:17,690 --> 00:13:18,400
Wrong.

238
00:13:19,190 --> 00:13:20,900
It wasn't her.

239
00:13:22,570 --> 00:13:26,400
So you basically burned an innocent woman alive?!

240
00:13:26,610 --> 00:13:28,030
Nice one!

241
00:13:28,030 --> 00:13:29,240
You're terrible!

242
00:13:29,240 --> 00:13:31,910
So, how did you explain it to her family?

243
00:13:31,910 --> 00:13:33,450
Did you cry and beg for mercy?

244
00:13:34,040 --> 00:13:37,210
Or did you perhaps refrain from saying anything because you were afraid of how furious they'd be?

245
00:13:37,370 --> 00:13:39,460
Were you never taught to shut your mouth, moron?!

246
00:13:41,920 --> 00:13:46,220
I'm starting to get tired of asking you homunculi the same question.

247
00:13:47,930 --> 00:13:50,340
Simply state the truth,

248
00:13:50,340 --> 00:13:51,220
you moron!

249
00:13:53,850 --> 00:13:55,890
Who killed Hughes?

250
00:14:11,870 --> 00:14:14,120
Congratulations, Colonel Mustang!

251
00:14:15,080 --> 00:14:17,330
You finally found the real culprit.

252
00:14:24,090 --> 00:14:28,010
I can't imagine Hughes getting killed by a moron like you.

253
00:14:29,720 --> 00:14:30,840
'Moron'?

254
00:14:32,010 --> 00:14:34,680
Morons are what you'd call...

255
00:14:34,680 --> 00:14:36,770
...idiots like Hughes...

256
00:14:38,850 --> 00:14:43,020
...who'd fall for dumb shit like this!

257
00:14:47,190 --> 00:14:49,070
Your face changed!

258
00:14:49,240 --> 00:14:51,280
I love that expression!

259
00:14:51,570 --> 00:14:54,870
Hughes had a great look on his face when I killed him too!

260
00:14:55,080 --> 00:14:57,660
Yeah, that face!

261
00:14:57,950 --> 00:15:02,120
The despair of being killed by someone who looks just like his beloved wife...

262
00:15:02,120 --> 00:15:04,000
It was just...

263
00:15:04,380 --> 00:15:05,880
...the best!

264
00:15:07,800 --> 00:15:08,920
It's decided.

265
00:15:11,380 --> 00:15:13,680
You're the one who killed Hughes.

266
00:15:13,680 --> 00:15:16,100
That's all I needed to know.

267
00:15:17,140 --> 00:15:19,480
You don't need to say anything else, Envy.

268
00:15:21,230 --> 00:15:23,900
Let's start this by...

269
00:15:25,650 --> 00:15:27,320
...reducing your tongue to ashes.

270
00:15:42,080 --> 00:15:43,290
Scar.

271
00:15:43,290 --> 00:15:44,210
Fullmetal.

272
00:15:44,580 --> 00:15:46,290
Leave this place to me.

273
00:15:48,460 --> 00:15:50,340
He's my prey.

274
00:15:53,090 --> 00:15:54,760
G-Gotcha.

275
00:15:54,760 --> 00:15:57,390
Well then, we'll leave this place to you and go on-

276
00:15:58,470 --> 00:16:01,430
Who gave you permission to pass?

277
00:16:01,850 --> 00:16:04,770
I still need to repay the debt you guys gave me up north-

278
00:16:08,020 --> 00:16:12,450
Do you have the time to be speaking to others while facing me?

279
00:16:13,780 --> 00:16:18,700
Seems like there's quite a lot of fat on that blabbering tongue of yours.

280
00:16:19,080 --> 00:16:21,950
It burns quite well, Envy.

281
00:16:21,950 --> 00:16:24,420
Lieutenant, will it really be okay-

282
00:16:24,420 --> 00:16:25,960
Go, Edward.

283
00:16:26,920 --> 00:16:28,460
We'll figure something out.

284
00:16:28,670 --> 00:16:29,750
But...

285
00:16:29,750 --> 00:16:31,920
Go, Edward Elric.

286
00:16:33,760 --> 00:16:36,140
Don't you have something you need to take care of?

287
00:16:37,550 --> 00:16:39,050
Come on, let's go, Ed.

288
00:16:39,050 --> 00:16:39,760
Hey-

289
00:16:46,650 --> 00:16:47,770
You son of a....!

290
00:16:48,480 --> 00:16:50,270
The Colonel will be fine.

291
00:16:51,650 --> 00:16:55,150
Finishing off a homunculus
should be a piece of cake for him.

292
00:16:55,610 --> 00:16:58,160
That's not the issue I'm worried about.

293
00:16:58,160 --> 00:16:59,030
Huh?

294
00:16:59,030 --> 00:17:00,240
Then what is?

295
00:17:03,620 --> 00:17:07,830
I see, so you've been seeking revenge for Hughes' death the entire time.

296
00:17:08,170 --> 00:17:11,750
What a beautiful friendship!

297
00:17:18,220 --> 00:17:19,720
Stay back, Lieutenant.

298
00:17:30,020 --> 00:17:35,530
Out of respect for that beautiful friendship, I'll fight you seriously.

299
00:17:35,740 --> 00:17:39,450
But I can't really hold back when fighting in this state.

300
00:17:39,450 --> 00:17:41,030
Don't blame me for any-

301
00:17:45,540 --> 00:17:49,000
How does it feel to have all the liquids within your eyes boil?

302
00:17:49,000 --> 00:17:51,170
The pain goes far beyond anything you could possibly imagine, doesn't it.

303
00:17:51,170 --> 00:17:52,170
You little-

304
00:17:57,090 --> 00:17:59,800
It was nice of you to make yourself a bigger target.

305
00:18:00,220 --> 00:18:02,720
Did you think you could beat me if you increased your size?

306
00:18:02,720 --> 00:18:03,810
Moron.

307
00:18:04,060 --> 00:18:05,600
Get up, monster.

308
00:18:05,600 --> 00:18:07,600
Hurry up and regenerate.

309
00:18:07,600 --> 00:18:10,310
I'll have you repeat this suffering until you're dead.

310
00:18:10,650 --> 00:18:12,020
That's...

311
00:18:12,020 --> 00:18:13,320
That's right.

312
00:18:13,770 --> 00:18:16,320
He's the one who burned Lust to death!

313
00:18:22,830 --> 00:18:23,620
Wait!

314
00:18:23,870 --> 00:18:24,740
Colonel!

315
00:18:24,740 --> 00:18:26,660
You wait here, Lieutenant!

316
00:18:26,660 --> 00:18:29,040
I'll dispose of him on my own!

317
00:18:36,800 --> 00:18:39,260
Yeah, I think it's this way.

318
00:18:39,930 --> 00:18:41,550
These things look creepy.

319
00:18:41,550 --> 00:18:43,350
They're almost like veins.

320
00:18:43,350 --> 00:18:47,220
I keep having this nasty feeling, like I'm having heartburn.

321
00:18:48,350 --> 00:18:49,560
Not surprising.

322
00:18:50,060 --> 00:18:53,690
There's a huge cluster of energy ahead.

323
00:18:54,480 --> 00:18:56,070
Cluster of energy?

324
00:18:56,530 --> 00:19:01,490
Would you get it if I described it as an insane number of people crawling about?

325
00:19:01,490 --> 00:19:05,870
Not really, but I do understand that it feels disgusting.

326
00:19:08,870 --> 00:19:12,040
I'd hate to encounter an enemy in a place like this.

327
00:19:15,090 --> 00:19:17,170
Scar, do you mind?

328
00:19:18,420 --> 00:19:20,670
Is this about the Flame Alchemist?

329
00:19:24,010 --> 00:19:30,680
Because I once lost my soul after engulfing myself in flames of revenge, I can understand well.

330
00:19:31,520 --> 00:19:34,440
If he goes on...

331
00:19:34,440 --> 00:19:38,690
...he'll end up reducing even his own heart with the flames of wrath.

332
00:19:54,540 --> 00:19:56,000
Where did you go, Envy?!

333
00:19:56,880 --> 00:19:58,050
Damn him...!

334
00:19:59,210 --> 00:20:02,680
If you don't come out, you'll be seeing another huge explosion from me!

335
00:20:05,640 --> 00:20:06,930
Yo, Roy.

336
00:20:07,970 --> 00:20:10,600
You're human after all! Let this throw you into confusion!

337
00:20:15,190 --> 00:20:20,360
You'd set your best friend aflame without hesitation?!

338
00:20:20,360 --> 00:20:22,150
Hughes is dead.

339
00:20:22,320 --> 00:20:23,610
He's no longer here.

340
00:20:23,900 --> 00:20:27,200
Your actions do nothing more than feeding oil to flames!

341
00:20:31,750 --> 00:20:33,330
Damn you!!

342
00:20:33,330 --> 00:20:35,580
Don't get so cocky!!

343
00:20:38,960 --> 00:20:40,050
Again...!

344
00:20:40,050 --> 00:20:43,550
My eyes... My eyes...!

345
00:20:43,550 --> 00:20:44,510
Fool.

346
00:20:44,970 --> 00:20:47,970
You came at me, thinking I wouldn't use much firepower if you were near me?

347
00:20:48,550 --> 00:20:50,930
Unfortunately for you, I can pinpoint.

348
00:20:50,930 --> 00:20:54,140
Don't you dare underestimate me!

349
00:21:00,610 --> 00:21:03,360
Colonel, I'm going to have to disobey your orders.

350
00:21:15,370 --> 00:21:16,710
He ran away again.

351
00:21:54,160 --> 00:21:56,410
You're disobeying my orders, Lieutenant.

352
00:21:56,410 --> 00:21:57,620
I apologize.

353
00:21:57,620 --> 00:21:59,960
But I couldn't just stand there and wait...

354
00:22:01,840 --> 00:22:02,840
Where is Envy?

355
00:22:03,300 --> 00:22:04,760
I lost him.

356
00:22:04,760 --> 00:22:06,090
This place is like a maze.

357
00:22:07,050 --> 00:22:09,220
Don't leave my side, Lieutenant.

358
00:22:09,840 --> 00:22:11,600
Now that you're here, I'm going to ask for your help.

359
00:22:39,250 --> 00:22:42,800
Ever since that day passed,

360
00:22:39,250 --> 00:22:42,800
Ano hi kara zutto

361
00:22:42,800 --> 00:22:47,050
I promised myself that I'd never cry.

362
00:22:42,800 --> 00:22:47,050
Nakanaito kimetekitakedo

363
00:22:47,590 --> 00:22:52,600
But even while I hoarded up the pain,

364
00:22:47,590 --> 00:22:52,600
Itami wo kasanetemo

365
00:22:52,600 --> 00:22:57,710
there was something I couldn't forgive myself for.

366
00:22:52,600 --> 00:22:57,710
Nanika wo yurusezu ni ita

367
00:22:59,190 --> 00:23:01,150
I'll never be able

368
00:22:59,190 --> 00:23:01,150
Mou modorenai

369
00:23:01,150 --> 00:23:03,650
to return to those days.

370
00:23:01,150 --> 00:23:03,650
Ikutsumo no hibi

371
00:23:03,650 --> 00:23:08,740
I'm still powerless.

372
00:23:03,650 --> 00:23:08,740
Boku wa mada nanimo dekizuni

373
00:23:08,740 --> 00:23:13,990
I watch as the shards of memories disappear, one by one;

374
00:23:08,740 --> 00:23:13,990
Kimi no ita kioku no kakera

375
00:23:13,990 --> 00:23:19,860
memories of when you were still with me.

376
00:23:13,990 --> 00:23:19,860
Mata hitotsu kieteyuku

377
00:23:20,540 --> 00:23:22,880
I long to become

378
00:23:20,540 --> 00:23:22,880
Kyou yori motto

379
00:23:22,880 --> 00:23:25,630
stronger than I am now,

380
00:23:22,880 --> 00:23:25,630
Tsuyoku naritai

381
00:23:25,630 --> 00:23:30,770
so that my voice will eventually reach you.

382
00:23:25,630 --> 00:23:30,770
Kono koe ga itsuka todokuyouni

383
00:23:30,770 --> 00:23:33,140
If the wind happens to stop

384
00:23:30,770 --> 00:23:33,140
Arukitsuzukete

385
00:23:33,140 --> 00:23:35,850
in the midst of my long journey,

386
00:23:33,140 --> 00:23:35,850
Kaze ga yandara

387
00:23:35,850 --> 00:23:40,560
I'll look up at the sky in search of you.

388
00:23:35,850 --> 00:23:40,560
Kimi wo sagashite sora miageruyo

389
00:23:41,310 --> 00:23:47,900
Beyond the daybreak, a ray of light breaks free.

390
00:23:41,310 --> 00:23:47,900
Yoake no saki ni hikari ga sasuyo

391
00:23:49,070 --> 00:23:53,450
A rainbow spans across the sky.

392
00:23:49,070 --> 00:23:53,450
Niji ga kakaruyo

393
00:23:59,330 --> 00:24:01,410
From the moment someone is born,

394
00:24:01,410 --> 00:24:05,290
they gradually become more and more human as time goes by.

395
00:24:05,960 --> 00:24:11,880
And what has been accumulated eventually becomes complete as a strong self.

396
00:24:12,340 --> 00:24:13,340
However...

397
00:24:14,590 --> 00:24:18,810
Next time, Fullmetal Alchemist:

398
00:24:18,810 --> 00:24:23,060
Episode 54, Beyond the Inferno.

399
00:24:18,830 --> 00:24:23,080
Beyond the Inferno

400
00:24:23,060 --> 00:24:26,610
Peer once more at your heart.
